{
  "bio": [
    "Apoorva Mehta is a cofounder of San Francisco-based grocery delivery firm Instacart, which went public on the Nasdaq under its legal name Maplebear in 2023.",
    "Mehta served as chairman and CEO for nearly a decade after cofounding the company in 2012. He stepped down as CEO in 2021 and chairman in 2023.",
    "He still owns about 7% of Maplebear's common stock plus options to acquire another 1% of the company.",
    "In 2022, private investors valued Mehta's new health-tech startup Cloud Health Systems at $200 million.",
    "Born in India, Mehta lived in Libya before moving to Canada, where he eventually studied engineering at the University of Waterloo."
  ],
  "about": [
    "Before founding Instacart, Mehta tried to create a product focused on social networking for lawyers.",
    "In Instacart's early days, orders often came in without a shopper available, so Mehta, who did not own a car, made the deliveries himself via Uber."
  ]
